<script setup lang="ts">
/**
 * ── Why these marks are inlined SVG and not <img src="/Silvicom*.svg"> ──────────────────────────
 * Both marks are two-tone by construction: navy shapes with the "360" KNOCKED OUT of them in
 * white. On a dark surface the <img> version was recoloured with `brightness-0 invert`, a filter
 * that cannot tell the two tones apart — it painted the navy white and the white knockout white
 * as well, so the 360 disappeared. The wordmark's badge became three blank discs and the S mark
 * lost its 360 entirely (measured 2026-08-29, both marks, on the shipped assets).
 *
 * Inline, each tone is a class, so dark mode swaps them instead of flattening them: the ink goes
 * white and the knockout takes the ink's navy, which is what an inverted two-tone mark should be.
 *
 * It also puts the mark on the app's real theming mechanism. There is no `.dark` class in
 * apps/web (D-DS2) — `color-scheme` on <html> plus `light-dark()` is the whole toggle — and
 * `light-dark()` inside this component resolves against exactly that. The filter it replaces read
 * a JS `isDark` that never subscribed to `matchMedia`, so a user on "system" who changed the OS
 * scheme with the app open kept the wrong mark until reload.
 *
 * The artwork itself is untouched: `public/SilvicomLogoText.svg` and `public/SilvicomLogoS.svg`
 * remain the source these were generated from — same geometry, same paint order, only the fills
 * became classes — and the S mark is still the favicon in `index.html`. Regenerate from those if
 * the brand files are ever revised.
 *
 * Size it from the parent, e.g. <AppLogo class="size-8" />.
 */
</script>

